Reason:
The driver was incorrectly handling the error codes sent by the chip during the firmware download process. Instead of responding with a NAK for timeout error codes, it was sending an ACK when there was no error, which caused the chip to ignore the firmware chunks and repeatedly resend the same bootloader signature with the error code.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
